{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In 2020, the population of a city was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a35e6e5aba16151c7777c80cda6b2ed4809adf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$415{,}638$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. The population decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb260f91e7c7a16a36a9d7c1dcfe44bc955ef756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> per year. Which function models the town's population <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff51845797a05fd68c53c81a189bc899dc2537b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=$\" width=\"29\" height=\"8\" /> number of years after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711f306f8ae87ce252ebd66c0926436e692236e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  P(x)=415638\\cdot(1.13)^x \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  P(x)=415638\\cdot(1.013)^x \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  P(x)=415638\\cdot(1.013)^{x-2020} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  P(x)=415638\\cdot(0.987)^{x-2020} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  P(x)=415638\\cdot(0.987)^x \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the population decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb260f91e7c7a16a36a9d7c1dcfe44bc955ef756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> per year, the rate would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938e0ee32338f4da1c64e936450f6abb1a9c930d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - 0.013 = 0.987$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" />. Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5e9307178eb149ef02ee36408f564223efbe73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> represents the population in the year <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so the power should be the number of years since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. This best matches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab1ceb4795ab493ace0f61dc42ed9ee4f447a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 415638 \\cdot (0.987)^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"178\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a>